################################################################################
# Cool URIs do not change: https://www.w3.org/Provider/Style/URI
#
# This file is the inventory of every URL scheme this site has answered to over
# twenty years of backends and generators, mapped back to today's canonical URLs.
# Tutorial and findings: https://kevin.deldycke.com/2022/cloudflare-commands#pages-redirects
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. The Pages engine only counts a rule as static while it
# appears BEFORE the first rule containing a * or :placeholder. From that rule on,
# every line burns the 100-dynamic budget, and at 101 the parser discards the REST
# OF THE FILE. This file lost its last 18 rules to that cliff for years. Hence the
# contract, enforced by tests/test_redirects.py against the engine replica in
# tests/pages_redirects_engine.py:
#
#   1. All exact rules first, all */:placeholder rules second.
#   2. The dynamic half stays under 100 rules.
#
# Matching is anchored: :name never crosses a slash and never matches empty, * may
# match empty. So /a and /a/ are different sources, and a rule ending in /* also
# answers the bare trailing-slash URL via an empty splat. WordPress URLs all ended
# in a slash, which is why the /* twins matter historically.
################################################################################

